<metadata><name>Heather Canyon Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:194-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.325400" lon="-121.635000"><ele>1380.0</ele><name>Hood River Meadows Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hood-river-meadows-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 196; book_elev_ft: 4477; quote: At Hood River Meadows Sno-Park climb the snow bank at the center of the north side and enter a wide lane into the forest</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.326668" lon="-121.637050"><ele>1384.7</ele><name>Foot of the Heather Canyon Trail</name><desc>source: south end of OSM way 542478568 Heather Canyon Trail (piste:type nordic); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 196; quote: enter a wide lane into the forest</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.345568" lon="-121.653406"><ele>1623.1</ele><name>Lower end of the upper canyon</name><desc>source: north end of OSM way 542478568, where the Heather Canyon Runout piste begins; confidence: low; pdf_page: 196; book_elev_ft: 5277; quote: About 2.2 miles from the sno-park the meadows end and you are standing at the lower end of the upper canyon ... Here you are 800 feet above your starting point</desc></wpt>
